## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest · **Tests:** 10 · **Production:** `ProductCatalog.cs` (10 public members)

---

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| 🔴 Critical | 2 (systemic — affects all 10 tests) |
| 🟡 Medium | 2 |
| Total | 4 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** suite. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called exactly once, hitting 95% line coverage, but **6 of 10 tests have zero assertions** and the remaining 4 assert only `IsNotNull` on types that can never be null. No test verifies that any operation produces a correct result. Every test will pass even if the production code is completely broken (e.g., `AddProduct` silently drops products, `ApplyBulkDiscount` doubles prices instead of discounting).

---

### 🔴 Critical #1 — Coverage-Touching / No Assertions (6 tests)

These tests call a method and return. They prove the method doesn't throw — nothing else.

| Test (line) | What it calls | What it asserts |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (17) | `AddProduct` | ∅ |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (33) | `UpdatePrice` | ∅ |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (39) | `RemoveProduct` | ∅ |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (64) | `GetProductCount` | ∅ |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (69) | `ApplyBulkDiscount` | ∅ |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (85) | `ImportFromCsv` | ∅ |

**Fix — example for each:**

```csharp
// AddProduct_Works → AddProduct_StoresProduct_RetrievableBysku
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct_RetrievableBySku()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(product, retrieved);
}

// UpdatePrice_Works → UpdatePrice_ChangesPrice
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ExistingProduct_UpdatesPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
}

// RemoveProduct_Works → RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnfindable
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_ExistingProduct_NoLongerFound()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}

// GetProductCount_Works → verify the count value
[TestMethod]
